# Frontend Testing Setup - Vitest & React Testing Library

## Overview
The DECM frontend uses **Vitest** for unit and integration testing, combined with **React Testing Library** for component testing and **MSW** (Mock Service Worker) for API mocking.

## Test Configuration

### Vitest Config
[apps/web/vitest.config.ts](mdc:apps/web/vitest.config.ts):

```typescript
test: {
  environment: 'happy-dom',      // Lightweight DOM environment
  globals: true,                  // Global test functions
  setupFiles: ['./src/test/setup.ts'],
  coverage: {
    provider: 'v8',
    reporter: ['text', 'json', 'html'],
    exclude: ['node_modules/', 'src/test/', '**/*.test.tsx', 'src/router.ts']
  },
  include: ['src/**/*.{test,spec}.{ts,tsx}']
}
```

### Test Environment
- **Environment**: `happy-dom` (lightweight jsdom alternative)
- **Globals**: Global test/describe/it functions available without imports
- **Setup File**: [src/test/setup.ts](mdc:apps/web/src/test/setup.ts) - Runs before tests

## Test Setup File

### Expected Setup
```typescript
// src/test/setup.ts
import '@testing-library/jest-dom';
import { afterEach } from 'vitest';
import { cleanup } from '@testing-library/react';

// Cleanup after each test
afterEach(() => {
  cleanup();
});

// Mock window.matchMedia (for responsive components)
Object.defineProperty(window, 'matchMedia', {
  writable: true,
  value: vi.fn().mockImplementation(query => ({
    matches: false,
    media: query,
    onchange: null,
    addListener: vi.fn(),
    removeListener: vi.fn(),
    addEventListener: vi.fn(),
    removeEventListener: vi.fn(),
    dispatchEvent: vi.fn(),
  })),
});
```

## Running Tests

### Test Commands
```bash
# Run all tests
pnpm test

# Run tests in watch mode (for development)
pnpm test --watch

# Run tests with coverage
pnpm test --coverage

# Run specific test file
pnpm test Button.test.tsx

# Run tests matching pattern
pnpm test --grep "handles click"

# Run tests with UI dashboard
pnpm test --ui
```

### Coverage Analysis
```bash
# Generate coverage report
pnpm test --coverage

# View HTML coverage report
# Open coverage/index.html in browser
```

**Coverage Targets**:
- Frontend: Minimum 70% coverage
- Critical paths: 100% coverage
- Utilities: 90%+ coverage

## Test File Structure

### Naming Conventions
- Unit tests: `ComponentName.test.tsx` or `function.test.ts`
- Integration tests: `Feature.integration.test.tsx`
- Co-located with source files

### Example Structure
```
src/
├── components/
│   ├── Button/
│   │   ├── Button.tsx
│   │   ├── Button.test.tsx        # Unit test
│   │   ├── Button.stories.tsx      # Storybook
│   │   └── index.ts
│   └── Form/
│       ├── Form.tsx
│       └── Form.test.tsx
├── hooks/
│   ├── useWalletAuth.ts
│   └── useWalletAuth.test.ts
├── pages/
│   ├── HomePage.tsx
│   └── HomePage.integration.test.tsx
└── test/
    ├── setup.ts                    # Test configuration
    └── mocks/
        ├── handlers.ts             # MSW handlers
        └── server.ts               # MSW server
```

## Component Testing Patterns

### Basic Component Test
```typescript
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import { Button } from './Button';

describe('Button', () => {
  it('renders button with text', () => {
    render(<Button>Click me</Button>);
    
    expect(screen.getByText('Click me')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('is disabled when disabled prop is true', () => {
    render(<Button disabled>Click me</Button>);
    
    expect(screen.getByRole('button')).toBeDisabled();
  });
});
```

### User Interaction Test
```typescript
import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event';

describe('Button', () => {
  it('calls onClick handler when clicked', async () => {
    const handleClick = vi.fn();
    const user = userEvent.setup();
    
    render(<Button onClick={handleClick}>Click me</Button>);
    
    await user.click(screen.getByRole('button'));
    
    expect(handleClick).toHaveBeenCalledOnce();
  });
});
```

### Form Submission Test
```typescript
describe('LoginForm', () => {
  it('submits form with valid data', async () => {
    const handleSubmit = vi.fn();
    const user = userEvent.setup();
    
    render(<LoginForm onSubmit={handleSubmit} />);
    
    await user.type(screen.getByLabelText('Email'), 'test@example.com');
    await user.type(screen.getByLabelText('Password'), 'password123');
    await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /submit/i }));
    
    expect(handleSubmit).toHaveBeenCalledWith({
      email: 'test@example.com',
      password: 'password123'
    });
  });
});
```

## API Mocking with MSW

### Setup MSW Server
```typescript
// src/test/mocks/server.ts
import { setupServer } from 'msw/node';
import { handlers } from './handlers';

export const server = setupServer(...handlers);
```

### Global Setup
```typescript
// src/test/setup.ts
import { beforeAll, afterEach, afterAll } from 'vitest';
import { server } from './mocks/server';

beforeAll(() => server.listen({ onUnhandledRequest: 'error' }));
afterEach(() => server.resetHandlers());
afterAll(() => server.close());
```

### Mock Handlers
```typescript
// src/test/mocks/handlers.ts
import { http, HttpResponse } from 'msw';

export const handlers = [
  http.post('/api/v1/auth/nonce', () => {
    return HttpResponse.json({ nonce: 'mock-nonce-123' });
  }),

  http.post('/api/v1/auth/verify', () => {
    return HttpResponse.json({
      user_id: 'user-123',
      wallet_address: '0x123...',
    });
  }),

  http.get('/api/v1/events', () => {
    return HttpResponse.json([
      {
        id: '1',
        name: 'Event 1',
        date: '2024-01-01',
      }
    ]);
  }),
];
```

### Testing with Mocked API
```typescript
describe('EventList', () => {
  it('displays events from API', async () => {
    render(<EventList />);
    
    // Wait for data to load
    const eventName = await screen.findByText('Event 1');
    
    expect(eventName).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('handles API error', async () => {
    server.use(
      http.get('/api/v1/events', () => {
        return HttpResponse.json(
          { error: 'Server error' },
          { status: 500 }
        );
      })
    );

    render(<EventList />);
    
    const errorText = await screen.findByText(/error/i);
    expect(errorText).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
```

## Hook Testing

### Testing Custom Hooks
```typescript
import { renderHook, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react';
import { useWalletConnection } from './useWalletConnection';

describe('useWalletConnection', () => {
  it('connects wallet successfully', async () => {
    const { result } = renderHook(() => useWalletConnection());
    
    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(result.current.isConnected).toBe(true);
    });
  });
});
```

### Testing with Context
```typescript
import { ReactNode } from 'react';
import { AuthProvider } from './AuthContext';

const wrapper = ({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) => (
  <AuthProvider>{children}</AuthProvider>
);

describe('useAuth hook', () => {
  it('provides auth context', () => {
    const { result } = renderHook(() => useAuth(), { wrapper });
    
    expect(result.current.isAuthenticated).toBeDefined();
  });
});
```

## Async Testing

### Waiting for Elements
```typescript
describe('AsyncComponent', () => {
  it('displays data after loading', async () => {
    render(<AsyncComponent />);
    
    // Wait for element to appear
    const element = await screen.findByText('Loaded data');
    expect(element).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('handles loading state', () => {
    render(<AsyncComponent />);
    
    // Loading state appears immediately
    expect(screen.getByText('Loading...')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
```

### Using waitFor
```typescript
import { waitFor } from '@testing-library/react';

it('updates state after async operation', async () => {
  render(<Component />);
  
  await waitFor(() => {
    expect(screen.getByText('Updated')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
```

## Accessibility Testing

### Testing Roles
```typescript
describe('Navigation', () => {
  it('has proper navigation structure', () => {
    render(<Navigation />);
    
    expect(screen.getByRole('navigation')).toBeInTheDocument();
    expect(screen.getAllByRole('link')).toHaveLength(3);
  });

  it('button has accessible label', () => {
    render(<IconButton icon="menu" ariaLabel="Open menu" />);
    
    expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Open menu' })).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
```

### Query Priorities
Use in order of preference:
1. `getByRole()` - Most accessible
2. `getByLabelText()` - For form inputs
3. `getByPlaceholderText()` - Last resort for inputs
4. `getByText()` - For text content
5. `getByTestId()` - Only for hard-to-query elements

## Snapshot Testing (Use Sparingly)

```typescript
it('renders correctly', () => {
  const { container } = render(<Component />);
  
  expect(container.firstChild).toMatchSnapshot();
});
```

**⚠️ Warning**: Use snapshots only for complex structures. Prefer specific assertions.

## Best Practices

### ✅ DO
- Test user interactions, not implementation details
- Use semantic queries (getByRole, getByLabelText)
- Mock external APIs with MSW
- Test accessibility
- Test error states and loading states
- Use descriptive test names
- Keep tests focused and isolated
- Mock only what's necessary

### ❌ DON'T
- Test implementation details
- Use shallow rendering
- Test third-party libraries
- Create shared test fixtures
- Use sleep/timeouts instead of waitFor
- Mock everything globally
- Test CSS styling (use visual testing instead)
- Skip cleanup between tests

